'''Yakov Kuzyakov''' is a soil scientist<ref name="ndiaeducationdiary">{{cite web |title=RUDN professor Yakov Kuzyakov is recognized as one of the most cited scientists in the world |url=https://indiaeducationdiary.in/rudn-professor-yakov-kuzyakov-is-recognized-as-one-of-the-most-cited-scientists-in-the-world/ |website=Indiaeducationdiary.in}}</ref><ref name="staff list">{{Cite web |title=Staff list of Institute of Soil Science |url=https://www.uni-goettingen.de/en/212970.html |access-date=2026-09-07 |website=uni-goettingen.de |language=en}}</ref> who works at the [[University of Göttingen]] at the Soil Science of Temperate Ecosystems department.<ref name="staff list" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Staff list of Institute of Soil Science of Temperate Ecosystems |url=https://www.uni-goettingen.de/en/team/81318.html |access-date=2022-04-01 |website=uni-goettingen.de |language=en}}</ref> He is also affiliated with the [[Patrice Lumumba Peoples' Friendship University of Russia|RUDN University]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://eng.rudn.ru/science/rudn-scientists/yakov-kuzyakov/|title=Yakov Kuzyakov|website=eng.rudn.ru}}</ref> Since September 2026 his work has been scrutinized, so far five of his papers have been retracted due to serious ethical violations during the peer review and editorial process.<ref name="Liang">{{cite journal |last1=Liang |first1=Qiong |last2=Chen |first2=Haiqing |last3=Gong |first3=Yuanshi |last4=Yang |first4=Hefa |last5=Fan |first5=Mingsheng |last6=Kuzyakov |first6=Yakov |title=RETRACTED: Effects of 15 years of manure and mineral fertilizers on enzyme activities in particle-size fractions in a North China Plain soil |journal=European Journal of Soil Biology |date=1 January 2014 |volume=60 |pages=112–119 |doi=10.1016/j.ejsobi.2013.11.009 |url=https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejsobi.2013.11.009|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref name="Maharjan">{{cite journal |last1=Maharjan |first1=Menuka |last2=Maranguit |first2=Deejay |last3=Kuzyakov |first3=Yakov |title=RETRACTED: Phosphorus fractions in subtropical soils depending on land use |journal=European Journal of Soil Biology |date=May 2018 |volume=87 |pages=17–24 |doi=10.1016/j.ejsobi.2018.04.002}}</ref><ref name="Qiu">{{cite journal |last1=Qiu |first1=Husen |last2=Zheng |first2=Xiaodong |last3=Ge |first3=Tida |last4=Dorodnikov |first4=Maxim |last5=Chen |first5=Xiangbi |last6=Hu |first6=Yajun |last7=Kuzyakov |first7=Yakov |last8=Wu |first8=Jinshui |last9=Su |first9=Yirong |last10=Zhang |first10=Zhenhua |title=RETRACTED: Weaker priming and mineralisation of low molecular weight organic substances in paddy than in upland soil |journal=European Journal of Soil Biology |date=November 2017 |volume=83 |pages=9–17 |doi=10.1016/j.ejsobi.2017.09.008}}</ref><ref name="Qiu2">{{cite journal |last1=Qiu |first1=Husen |last2=Ge |first2=Tida |last3=Liu |first3=Jieyun |last4=Chen |first4=Xiangbi |last5=Hu |first5=Yajun |last6=Wu |first6=Jinshui |last7=Su |first7=Yirong |last8=Kuzyakov |first8=Yakov |title=RETRACTED: Effects of biotic and abiotic factors on soil organic matter mineralization: Experiments and structural modeling analysis |journal=European Journal of Soil Biology |date=January 2018 |volume=84 |pages=27–34 |doi=10.1016/j.ejsobi.2017.12.003}}</ref><ref name="Wu">{{cite journal |last1=Wu |first1=Cuiyan |last2=Huang |first2=Wei |last3=Liu |first3=Yixian |last4=Li |first4=Han |last5=Ding |first5=Shuai |last6=Zhu |first6=Zhenke |last7=Wang |first7=Feng |last8=Dijkstra |first8=Feike A. |last9=Zhang |first9=Guangbin |last10=Kuzyakov |first10=Yakov |last11=Cheng |first11=Weiguo |last12=Xiao |first12=Mouliang |last13=Ge |first13=Tida |title=RETRACTED: Physicochemically protected organic carbon release is the rate-limiting step of rhizosphere priming in paddy soils |journal=Science of the Total Environment |date=10 December 2024 |volume=955 |article-number=176859 |doi=10.1016/j.scitotenv.2024.176859 |pmid=39414056 }}</ref>

== Research and career ==
He was a professor at the department of Agroecosystem Research at the [[University of Bayreuth]] until 2011.<ref>{{cite web |title=Yakov Kuzyakov |url=https://www.bayceer.uni-bayreuth.de/bayceer/de/mitarbeiter/mit/mitarbeiter_detail.php?id_obj=37830 |website=University of Bayreuth-BAYCEER |access-date=2026-10-08 }}</ref> Since 2011, he has headed the department of Soil Science of Temperate Ecosystems and the department of Agricultural Soil Science at the [[University of Göttingen]].<ref name="staff list" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Staff list of Institute of Soil Science |url=https://www.uni-goettingen.de/en/team/86014.html |access-date=2022-04-01 |website=uni-goettingen.de |language=en |archive-date=2022-03-31 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220331234716/https://www.uni-goettingen.de/en/team/86014.html }}</ref>

== Controversies ==
In 2026, his work came under scrutiny for unethical behavior. As an editor for the [[Elsevier]] European Journal of Soil Biology, he edited several of his own papers. As of September 2026, four of the papers in that journal that he authored and edited himself were retracted. Aside from editing four of his own papers,<ref name="Liang" /><ref name="Maharjan" /><ref name="Qiu" /><ref name="Qiu2" /> three papers had also been reviewed by at least one reviewer closely linked to him, compromising the editorial process.<ref>{{cite web |title=Retraction Watch Database |url=https://retractiondatabase.org/RetractionSearch.aspx#?auth%3dKuzyakov%252c%2bYakov |website=retractiondatabase.org}}</ref><ref name="Maharjan" /><ref name="Qiu" /><ref name="Qiu2" /> A fifth paper he authored in a second Elsevier journal, [[Science of the Total Environment]], was retracted due to suspicious changes in authors on the paper during the review process.<ref name="Wu" />

== Scientific achievements ==
Yakov is one of the most cited scientists in the world and has published more than a thousand scientific papers throughout his career.<ref name="ndiaeducationdiary" /><ref>{{Cite web|language=en|url=https://publons.com/researcher/1303239/yakov-kuzyakov/|title=Yakov Kuzyakov's Web of Sciece profile|website=publons.com|access-date=2020-08-20}}</ref> He has been a world's top 2% ranked scientists for 7 years straight since 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://manuelgarcia.info/worlds-top-scientists/author/28185940586|title=World'stop 2% scientists|website=manuelgarcia.info}}</ref> He was a highly cited researcher in the field of Agricultural Sciences between 2015 and 2020,<ref>{{Cite web|language=de|url=https://www.goettinger-tageblatt.de/Campus/Goettingen/Internationales-Ranking-viel-zitierte-Goettinger-Wissenschaftler|title=Viel zitierte Göttinger Wissenschaftler|website=GT - Göttinger Tageblatt|date=19 February 2018 |access-date=2020-08-20}}</ref> and was included in the list of the most cited Russian scientists in 2017.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Самые высокоцитируемые российские ученые 2017 года|author=Ирина Смазневич|url=https://4science.ru/articles/Samie-visoko-citiruemie-rossiiskie-uchenie-2017-goda|website=4science|date=2018-02-21}}</ref> Four of his papers published in [[Soil Biology and Biochemistry]] have been listed as the most cited over the last 50 years.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.journals.elsevier.com/soil-biology-and-biochemistry/article-selections/fifty-years-of-sbb-the-most-cited-articles-for-each-year|title=Fifty years of SBB: The most cited articles for each year - Article Selections: Virtual Special Issues - Soil Biology and Biochemistry - Journal - Elsevier|website=www.journals.elsevier.com}}</ref>

== Research interests ==
Kuzyakov specialises in [[soil ecology]] and soil [[biogeochemistry]] ([[lipids]], low molecular organic substances), [[agriculture]], land use, [[agroecology]], [[Carbon cycle|C]] and [[Nitrogen cycle|N cycles]], [[Priming (microbiology)|priming effects]], soil-plant interactions ([[rhizosphere]] processes), in-depth study of rhizodeposition, partitioning of CO<sub>2</sub> fluxes from soil and application of radioactive and stable isotope labelling approaches in soil science.<ref name="staff list" /><ref name="ndiaeducationdiary" />

